+## Sales and variance routes
+
+- `POST /import/sales` accepts `{ "csv": "ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty\n..." }`.
+  `soldAt` is an ISO instant with a timezone; `qty` is a positive whole number
+  of portions. Returns `{ "tickets": 1, "dishes": 2 }`, counting newly
+  imported tickets and total dish portions. Previously imported tickets are
+  skipped. Invalid rows or insufficient stock reject the whole file with
+  `sales_row`, naming the physical CSV row (header is row 1).
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` returns an array of
+  `{ "itemId": 1, "theoretical": 0.6, "actual": 0.8, "variance": 0.2 }`.
+  Both days are inclusive in UTC. Actual use includes every consume movement;
+  variance is actual minus theoretical use. Only items with positive use are
+  included, sorted by item id. Reversed ranges are rejected.
+
